description:
GAC Motor, a leading Chinese automotive group, is expanding in Mexico, and we are looking for a PR to join our dynamic team! If you’re passionate about the automotive industry and eager to contribute to a growing global brand, this is your opportunity.




Objective: Overall responsibility for public relations and brand communications of the Marketing Department of the subsidiary. The role receives the brand communication strategy and external messaging guidelines from headquarters, coordinates local media, PR agencies and the official social media matrix, drives brand communication, corporate publicity, public-opinion monitoring and PR events, and safeguards and enhances the image and reputation of the GAC brand in the Mexican market.




Responsabilities:




Brand communication planning: Develop the annual PR communication plan for the overseas brand and define the themes and creative direction for major corporate events; draft communication strategy proposals in line with the stage of the brand globalisation and safeguard the tone of international communications.
Corporate publicity: Oversee corporate-level external publicity content; identify and articulate the brand technical heritage and corporate culture; draft and review Chinese/English corporate press releases, executive interview outlines and official statements, ensuring consistent and authoritative corporate messaging.
PR communication planning and execution: Lead the implementation of core PR programmes; build and maintain a database of key overseas media relationships; manage the daily operation of the official overseas social media matrix; review all graphic and video content released through official channels.
 Public-opinion monitoring and crisis management: Build a public-opinion monitoring system with real-time tracking of overseas media and social platforms; establish a crisis early-warning mechanism, respond rapidly to sudden negative coverage, formulate PR solutions and follow through on implementation to protect brand reputation.
 PR event planning and execution: Plan and execute PR events, including but not limited to new model launches, media fleets and dealership openings.




Profile

 Bachelor degree or above; majors in public relations, journalism and communication, marketing, advertising or international communication are preferred;
 3-5 years or more of experience in public relations, brand communication or media communication; experience in the automotive industry, with a multinational brand or in overseas markets is preferred;
 Able to independently draft Chinese/English press releases, official statements and executive interview materials, with English as a working language; 
 Familiar with the overseas mainstream media landscape and the operating rules of social platforms (Facebook, Instagram, X, TikTok, YouTube, LinkedIn), as well as local media editorial preferences and publishing procedures;
 Strong capability in developing and maintaining media relationships; able to independently handle media invitations, interview arrangements, content review and publication follow-up;
 Hands-on experience in public-opinion monitoring and crisis PR; able to assess situations quickly, formulate solutions and drive cross-departmental implementation under pressure;
 Experience in managing PR agencies and vendors; familiar with budget preparation, project acceptance and expense settlement procedures;
 Strong cross-cultural communication, cross-departmental coordination and writing skills; rigorous and detail-oriented with a strong sense of confidentiality.

KPIs

 Completion rate of the annual PR communication plan and dedicated communication programmes;
 Number of key media covered, share of positive coverage and achievement of brand communication volume;
 Content output volume and interaction growth of the official social media matrix;
 Public-opinion monitoring coverage, response time to negative coverage and completion rate of crisis handling;
 Completion rate of PR events, and media attendance and coverage achieved;
 Compliance rate of PR budget execution and timeliness of project expense settlement.







